WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.860
Y'know, being a boat owner isn't all it's cracked up to be.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.520
I didn't even pay for this,
and I'm already having buyer's remorse.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.540
Well, the engine's still running.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.140
Yeah, easy.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.820
Yeah, and I don't even have to deal with licence
registration, docking fees, and it already—

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.400
It feels like a burden.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.020
Ah, shouldn't overthink it.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.200
I'll run out of gas at some point,
then the problem will solve itself.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.600
Dammit, how did they not know the river was dried up?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.480
When the whole plan hinges upon the river,
how do you miss that?

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.300
Wait, what am I doing?

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.040
I don't—

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.760
I guess I'm on foot.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.100
If I go back, it's just that dead woman.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.740
CIA bailed on me...

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.340
I guess I could try those apartments in the distance.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.420
But I haven't seen anyone.
They're not going to have any food.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.620
Just more bleach.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.200
I could try following supply guy,
might lead me to the nearest town...

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.940
But he had that bot following him.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.020
They've probably already sent troops there and are
rounding up people to be shot looking for him.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.000
This is really frustrating, because
I'm still in the dark on so many things!

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.640
So all I can do is try to guess
which person is least likely to get me killed.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.460
If the person dies, that doesn't help.
That just means they're wrong.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.740
There have been a lot of wrong guesses today.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.980
All roads lead to incompetence.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.140
Yeah, here's the problem, it's this giant gap.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.620
If that was filled in, I could almost make it...?

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.760
Y'know, just enough to get the front end on the ledge,
so I can flip the boat backwards with me in it.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.840
I feel like I'm just not gonna have closure on this,
unless I total the boat.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.560
I just need to extend the ramp.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.880
Oh hey, besides cash and a map,
how about a multi-tool?

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.280
They couldn't have given me that?

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.960
Oh, well there's a big log there, but I can't secure that.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.200
Yeah, a multi-tool is what? Ten bucks for a cheap one?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.100
Though really, I deserve an expensive one.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.200
Oh, there's some boards.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.780
Yeah, those were tough.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.180
Now I'm feeling a little shortsighted about
smashing them into pieces.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.560
It's almost as if you have more options
when you don't destroy everything.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:03.500
Almost.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:04.480
[wood creaking]

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.440
Oh, yeah, these'll work.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.760
Yeah, I'm still coming out ahead with the boat
than if I had just walked.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.920
I have another ten or twenty minutes before I'm tied,
so I can give this one more go.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:22.960
They say the captain always goes down the ship,
but being a boat owner, I think that's just the politically
correct version that's been passed down.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.660
As a captain, I kinda feel like if my boat goes down,
I want everyone to go down with it.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.060
You need something to commemorate it, y'know?

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.720
I guess any stowaways could jump off,
they were never really invested.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.120
I don't have any crew or passengers, though.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.060
If that supply guy comes back,
I'll ask him to come down here.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.540
Okay... this is an issue.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.260
The board's too long, the nails aren't gonna line up.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.760
Okay, I'll do it the classic way.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.360
Diagonal here should be fine.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.160
Uh...

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.040
Yeah, that looks good.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.500
Just set it there...

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.180
Oh yeah, that's perfect.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.460
This is the complete inverse of my old job.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:08.020
Before this, I had to come up with a
model for transmitting energy
along a pseudo-Riemannian manifold.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:11.320
That was trickier than this, but it was all theory.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.240
Here, it's "rotate the board."

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.660
But I have to actually go and do it.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.080
Well, my old job doesn't exist anymore, so there.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.900
Y'know, I don't even know if I'm gonna be missed
if I don't show up at... wherever they told me to go.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:29.000
If this doesn't work, then everyone involved has
more or less sentenced me to exile,

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.900
wandering the countryside, looking for food and water.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.260
I mean, would they send someone to find me?

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.260
Maybe.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.680
Would they die within two hours?

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.480
Eh...

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.160
So there's a chance, months from now,

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:48.760
some scout stumbles upon an old abandoned house,
and finds me wrapped up in an old blanket,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:54.620
eating canned tuna, growing a ZZ Top beard,
and they're like: "Freeman, is that you?"

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.580
And I say, "Yeah. Fuck you."

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.160
Ah, who am I kidding? Months...

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.540
It takes years to grow a beard like that.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.380
Hmm...

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.220
I say everyone's incompetent,
but there's more going on here than that.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:11.660
Like, I assume the CIA guy
had some mission he drafted me for.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:12.520
So that's...

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.120
Yeah, that looks about right.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.180
So when he dropped me off with no instructions,
no supplies, and no information,

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.100
I thought that was incompetent.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:20.980
Dut!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:21.960
Dah!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.840
It's obvious now I'm some sort of decoy, but even then,
I'd be more effective with a fake objective.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.820
Okay, that's about as good as it's gonna get.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.540
I should strength test this.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.980
I'll just do a quick jump.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:36.900
Hup.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.180
Yep. Seems—

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:38.680
Shit!

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.240
[vocalizing underwater]

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.400
Yeah, that passes inspection, I guess.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:50.340
But yeah, I thought CIA was doing that thing
every manager I've ever had does,

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:57.620
where he assumed because I did something successfully, no matter how much of an utter miracle it was that involved a lot of variables,

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.440
and probably isn't reproducible at all,

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.900
that I'll do that every time.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.800
So from his perspective...

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:09.300
it makes perfect sense to send me
into the lion's den with nothing.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.740
I survived Black Mesa, therefore, I'll survive anything.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.860
That's my defining trait as an employee.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.060
Why would I need additional resources?

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:22.660
The problem, of course, is they can't understand the flaw
in this reasoning until failure occurs.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.040
So, in my case, he can't learn unless I die.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.040
Well, class may be in session!

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.460
Ohhhh!

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.500
Oof!

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.140
Oh my god!

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.580
That worked!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:37.500
Oh... I better not have this exact
same situation in five minutes.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.600
Ah, yes, the beautiful c—

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.660
[coughing]

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.600
Fuck!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.100
OH!

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.440
What is that?!

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.360
Pretty sure that's not a friend!

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.500
I probably shouldn't be following it!

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.840
There's another reason not to take the river!

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.120
My options are kinda one-dimensional!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.520
It's not even a river!

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.860
I'm being tricked over and over again!

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.540
I can't trust anyone!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.240
Oh, for god's sake!

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.580
I'm not stopping! I'm not stopping!

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:04.320
Ah!

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.800
What did you do to my boat?!

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.880
Pirates trying to board me...!

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.000
Can barely steer this thi—

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:11.500
NO!

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.180
Get out of my lane!

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.340
This is my lane!

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:14.840
Metrocop: "Shit!"

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:15.340
[splat]

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.960
I was here first!

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.460
I have the right of way!

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.220
You don't even have a boat!

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.340
Go back to lifeguard duty!

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.240
You're not even dressed for water!

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.520
Oh my god, are you kidding me?

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.860
Yeah, put the logs up, so I can't—

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.960
Wait, that's a ramp. Maybe...?

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.980
Well, I'm not spending ten minutes here
building another one!

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:38.100
This was such a bad idea.
I shouldn't have listened to anyone!

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.280
Yeah, that's sort of a ramp. Gun it!

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.300
To the right...!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.440
No, I can't steer this!

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.680
WAAAHHH!

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.180
Oof!

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:46.420
[weak breathing]

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.940
Okay, that almost worked...

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.800
We obviously just need more speed!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.380
That's not a problem.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.420
Speed is my middle name!

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:56.920
In fact...

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:57.800
[Metropolice chatter]
In fact...

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.220
What, you're still here?

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.060
Don't make me come over there!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.060
You better not be here when I get back.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.280
Okay, this is it!

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:05.140
Go! Go!

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.480
It's working!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.220
It's wo—

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:07.860
[crash]

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.720
AAAHHH!

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.220
[thud]

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.780
Oh my god, there's more of them!

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:16.520
Yeah, attack me from the bridge,
that's actually a great vantage point!

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.720
That's how I would try to kill me too!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:19.620
Shit!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:20.120
[crash]

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:20.620
Ugh!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.300
Fuckin' swamp boat! I can't—

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.020
No!

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:25.080
Neugh!

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:26.200
Oof!

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.300
I need to get out of here...

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:28.860
No, no—

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.260
Back, back...

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.160
Come on!

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:32.120
Okay, okay.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.440
Now forward, and don't veer off—

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.580
Jesus Christ!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.540
Guess that's the good fishing spot.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:39.600
Fish...

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.140
Man, this is really shallow.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.900
Well the grass is green, I don't think it's drought.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.880
This has been drained. It's like the Colorado River.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:51.520
There must be some massive
irrigation project going on.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:53.520
Or hey, you know what? They're aliens.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.560
They could be using the—

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:55.940
Ah, shit.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:59.220
Okay, good. We have a stormtrooper in training here.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.500
Yeah, I see you. Bye.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.220
Why can't the whole day be—

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:04.660
[thud]
WHOA! Whoa!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.560
Whoa...

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.320
Oof!

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.620
Oh, jeez, side...

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.320
Ugh!

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.380
Turn!

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.320
Oh, no, no, no, no, no...

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.100
Okay, here's what's gonna happen:

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:16.040
I'm gonna gently nudge the gate open...

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.480
Okay, a little harder.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.100
Oof!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:19.860
Fuck!

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.940
We really haven't had enough of this bullshit?!

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.900
They sent me to a canal lock!

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:24.520
[gunfire]

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.060
[gunfire]
OH!

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.800
I'm boxed in!

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:27.380
Ngh!

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.700
Darth Uzi returns!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.000
Okay, that's it, that's it, I'm getting out.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.240
Boat ride's over.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:33.900
Oof...

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.300
Now it's time for the bullet ride!

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.320
Get ready, this one's a lot faster!

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.200
Oh what the fuck? Now he's getting sneaky on me.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.920
Well, he missed me fifty times,
and now I'm coming for him;

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.400
I'd fall back too.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:51.700
So, either he's smarter than he aims, or...
he left to go get more ammo.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:55.820
I'm sure there's more close by,
I mean, why wouldn't there be?

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.580
Dammit, where is he?

00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:00.020
Of course, he's gonna play mind games now.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:06.080
I'm half-expecting a cardboard cutout of him to spring out when I turn the corner, but still no sign of him.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:09.000
I hate those life-size cardboard cutouts.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.900
I remember attacking them
by accident at the shoe store.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.680
So what—

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:13.600
Ah!

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.940
Oh, that was bad.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:19.440
He shot first! That is not how we do things now!

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.820
I'm slipping!

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:25.800
The thing is, my freak-out-o-meter has never
really gone down this entire time,

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.160
but I can't be 100% vigilant at all times!

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:29.660
I just—

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.820
I need drugs!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:34.440
So this goes nowhere! That's nice!

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.060
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—direct
confirmation of a disruptor—"

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:36.560
Wha—

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.800
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—in our midst,"

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.300
What?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.900
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—one who has acquired an almost
messianic reputation in the minds—"

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:42.860
'Messianic'?

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:43.900
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—of certain citizens."

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.680
Is this the voice of God?

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.060
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—with the darkest urges of
instinct, ignorance and decay."

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.860
Okay, I'm definitely hearing voices,
that's not where I want it to go.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.600
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "have been laid
directly at his feet, and yet—"

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.900
What the hell?

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.380
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—continue
to imbue him with romantic—"

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.800
Oh, it's a satellite.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.780
Dr.Breen [faintly]: "—giving him such dangerous—"

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:05.100
But wait, I wouldn't hear the transmission...

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.900
Dr. Breen [faintly]: "—as the One Free Man,
the Opener of the Way."

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.520
'Opener of the Way'...

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.080
Oh, it's not locked!

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.540
Dr. Breen: "—the dangers of magical thinking."

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.380
Oh, it's this stupid—

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.500
Dr. Breen: "—from the dark pit—"

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.380
Acoustics...

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.320
Is there anyone there?

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.940
Dr. Breen: "Let us not slide backward into—"

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.220
There could be...

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.240
Dr. Breen: "—just as we have 
finally begun to see the light."

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:25.740
Dr. Breen: "If you see—"

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:28.700
Man, computers look even more hostile now.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.260
I bet this is Linux.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:33.600
Dr. Breen: "—do not go unrewarded, and contrariwise,"

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.200
Ah, he's not saying anything important.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.440
Is someone there?

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.200
Dr. Breen: "—will not go unpunished."

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.360
But I guess this is the only entertainment
I'm gonna get for a while.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.200
Dr. Breen: "Be safe."

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.820
Yes, be safe.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.160
Dr. Breen: "Be aware."

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.000
Aware. Yes, that is good advice.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.540
Oh, there is more ammo!

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.120
I would've missed that!

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.040
Maybe I should watch more of that show.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.220
It looked pretty dry, but maybe he has some good ideas.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.840
Idea men.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:04.120
Oh, speaking of which, I thought CIA was just
displaying classic manager syndrome,

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.900
but now I'm thinking there's more layers to it.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:10.000
Oh, fuck! That's one of those chairs
they were gonna put me in!

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.080
I knew it!

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.580
Y'know, that says something about that Barney guy!

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.120
Sure, he spared me for Kleiner,
but what's he doing the rest of the time?

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.020
Pulling teeth, probably!

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:21.100
He might be a fuckin' psycho!

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:21.940
Oh!

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:25.880
He was hiding behind a barrel!

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.860
The TV was trying to tell me!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.120
'Be aware'!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.560
Time to raise awareness!

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:35.400
God, I hate it when they pop out of barrels, and...

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.700
crates...

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:37.780
my dreams...

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.300
Jack-in-the-box warfare.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.360
I guess that's an interesting way to go:

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:47.800
Jump out at someone going "Hoo-hoo-HEH-HEH!" and
watch them freak out and shoot you in the head.

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:48.840
Don't look at me!

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:50.660
Yeah.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.800
There's too many surprises today.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.300
A lot of people start dying
once they exceed my surprise threshold.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.060
They're all bad, too.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.480
Nobody's going, "Oh hey, here, have a cake."

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.500
Oh, this is one of their vehicles.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.220
Does it open?

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:03.860
[buzzer]

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:04.960
Sure doesn't.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:05.460
Oh—

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.500
Yeah, that's exactly the kind of surprise I mean.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.320
It's not even a surprise now.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:13.160
I see one!

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:17.880
I thought I saw—

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:21.780
Yeah, I did.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:25.340
Man, there's a lot of cops here,
and they have equipment set up.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.480
They didn't arrive twenty minutes ago!

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.900
There's computers, cameras, interrog—

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.540
This is a full-fledged outpost!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.520
Christ, do we put in enough of these things?

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:36.340
Nyah!

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.880
The Underground Railroad leads
straight to a police outpost!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.200
Dammit, there's another behind the door there.
I'm seeing sparks.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.400
Maybe it's like that bucket of water trick.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:49.120
Instead of getting wet, you get a face full of saw blades.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.000
Ah...?!

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:50.900
Oh my god...

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.120
No... no...!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.460
I didn't imagine it!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.640
It's still there!

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:55.140
HA!

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:56.940
See?

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.840
Alright, now it's safe—𝙚𝙧 to move forward.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:05.000
Man, I need one of those little
sticks with the mirrors on them.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.740
I wanted one of those even before all this went down.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.200
'Be safe.'

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.500
'Be aware.'

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.060
Hey, what is this?

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.080
Oh my god! Grenades!

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.240
I'm taking 'em all!

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.520
I'm so excited!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:18.880
So, who's first?

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.240
Uh...

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:25.280
Okay, I'll put the pin back in, but...
it's good to have that in my hip pocket.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.360
Or, more like my entire waist.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.320
[gunfire]
AHHH! AHHH!

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.100
What's up with these smart tactics all of a sudden?!

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:34.600
I like the old you better!

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:39.980
The old you wouldn't have set up a machine gun nest
fifty yards away to cover the only access point!

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.460
You've changed!

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:44.640
But I know someone who hasn't changed. Not really.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.180
GRENAAAADE!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.200
Did it work?

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:49.060
[explosion]
GRENA—

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.300
Oh, there it goes.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.140
They were well-prepared.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.400
[explosion]

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.740
That just means there's
layers of wrongness going on here.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:14:01.000
The Resistance is completely screwed;
they're being hunted down like rabbits,

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.120
but the establishment is stupid too!

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.120
They're too aggressive!
They're working against themselves!

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.120
Someone back there?

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:09.160
No.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:10.620
I mean, they already have the—

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:11.120
[Metropolice chatter]
I mean, they already have the—

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:11.680
Woah!

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:13.420
Okay.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.000
Hi, it's me, GRENAAAADE!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.100
Metrocop: "Get down!"

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:19.420
[explosion]

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:21.620
Look out, GRENAAAADE!

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:22.980
Metrocop: "That's a grenade!"

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:23.540
Sure is!

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:24.040
[explosion]
Sure is!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.480
GRENAAAADE!

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:26.720
Metrocop: "Grenade!"

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:27.540
I know, right?

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:28.360
[explosion]

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.080
The Greeks say moderation in all things. I'm not Greek!

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:32.040
GRENA—

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:33.700
Oh, okay.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.920
Well, it's not fun if nobody else is playing.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.940
This is really a multiplayer thing.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.100
Yeah, these guys look partied out.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.200
But yeah, they had the perfect setup.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:46.620
Lead the Resistance down the canal,
then interrogate and kill them once they arrive here.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:47.800
More grenades!

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.120
Well, if you insist!

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:56.300
And this place is outside the city, so you can kill all
Resistance and keep it quiet so you don't tip them off.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.820
They'll just keep coming.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:01.240
So why on earth would you attack this route?

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:06.120
That's like smashing roaches on their way
to the roach motel, causing them all to scatter.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.920
This isn't rocket science.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:08.980
I should know.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.480
This is the blind fighting the blind.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:12.460
[crow call]

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:12.960
AHHH!

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:14.840
[growl]

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.700
Yeah, that's right. Tell them I sent you.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.900
Wait, this is just another dead end?

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:20.620
[exasperated stammer]

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.620
This is getting really old!

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:25.100
This is slowing me down a lot too!

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:27.020
Oh, this opens the lock!

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:28.640
Wait, that has live current!

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:30.180
That could kill me!

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:34.420
If there's anything I've learned from the aliens,
it's don't get electrocuted.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.180
So, uh...

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.460
Yeah, this is bullshit.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.280
Y'know, it's true what they say:

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.120
Owning a boat is a trap.

